sentences.t:
Qualis saepe viae deprensus in aggere serpens,
aerea quem obliquum rota transiit, aut gravis ictu
seminecem liquit saxo lacerumque viator;

sentences.l:
As often on the road's causeway caught a snake,
bronze-tyred whom crosswise a wheel has passed over, or heavy with a blow
half-dead has left with a stone, and mangled, a wayfarer;
